# Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request".
# Run `npm run seed` first. Every seeded account uses the password Password@123.
@api = http://localhost:3000/api

### ---------- Phase 1: basics ----------

### Health check: expect 200 { "ok": true }
GET {{api}}/health

### Unknown route: expect 404 with the shared error shape
GET {{api}}/does-not-exist

### Broken JSON body: expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{api}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{ "oops":

### ---------- Phase 3: auth ----------

### Register a new user: expect 201 with a token and a generated upiId
# (Run it twice: the second time expect 400 "already registered".)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test User", "email": "test.user@example.com", "password": "Password@123" }

### Register with bad input: expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with details
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short" }

### Log in as Priya (normal user). The token is saved for the requests below.
# @name priya
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "priya@sandbox.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

### Wrong password: expect 401 "Invalid email or password"
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "priya@sandbox.dev", "password": "wrong-password" }

### Who am I? (with Priya's token): expect 200 and her profile, no passwordHash
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### Who am I? (no token): expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Who am I? (tampered token): expect 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}x

### Admin route as Priya: expect 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{api}}/rules
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### Log in as the admin
# @name admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@sandbox.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

### Admin route as admin: expect 200 with the 3 rules
GET {{api}}/rules
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.token}}

### ---------- Phase 4: wallet, lookup, history ----------
# These reuse Priya's token: run "Log in as Priya" above first.

### Wallet: balance and today's spend (paise)
GET {{api}}/wallet
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### Top up ₹500 (50000 paise)
POST {{api}}/wallet/topup
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 50000 }

### Top up over ₹50,000: expect 400
POST {{api}}/wallet/topup
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 5000001 }

### Look up a receiver: expect { name: "Ravi Kumar" } and nothing else
GET {{api}}/users/lookup?upiId=ravi@sandbox
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### Look up someone who doesn't exist: expect 404
GET {{api}}/users/lookup?upiId=nobody@sandbox
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### History: page 1, newest first
GET {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### History: only successful, 3 per page, page 2
GET {{api}}/transfers?status=success&limit=3&page=2
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### Log in as Ravi (his seed data has a blocked attempt)
# @name ravi
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ravi@sandbox.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

### History: Ravi's blocked attempts only: expect 1 row with ruleHit VELOCITY
GET {{api}}/transfers?status=blocked
Authorization: Bearer {{ravi.response.body.token}}

### History: a date range (edit the dates to match your seed run)
GET {{api}}/transfers?from=2026-10-06&to=2026-10-08
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### History: bad filter values: expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{api}}/transfers?status=pending&from=yesterday
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}

### ---------- Phase 5: transfers and the fraud engine ----------
# Run `npm run seed` first for a clean slate. Uses Priya's token from above.
# Amounts are in paise: ₹2,000 = 200000.

### 1. Normal transfer to an old friend (Priya has paid Ravi before): expect 201
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "ravi@sandbox", "amount": 200000, "note": "Chai" }

### 2. New payee over the cap (₹25,000 to Karan, never paid): expect 403 NEW_PAYEE_CAP
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "karan@sandbox", "amount": 2500000 }

### 3. Over the daily limit (₹49,000 more to Ravi after the ₹2,000 above): expect 403 DAILY_LIMIT
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "ravi@sandbox", "amount": 4900000 }

### 4. Velocity: send this ₹10 transfer 3 more times quickly; the 4th within 60s is blocked
# (Request 1 above counts if it was in the last minute.)
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "anita@sandbox", "amount": 1000 }

### Hard check: to yourself: expect 400
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "priya@sandbox", "amount": 1000 }

### Hard check: unknown receiver: expect 404
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "nobody@sandbox", "amount": 1000 }

### Hard check: decimal paise: expect 400
POST {{api}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toUpiId": "ravi@sandbox", "amount": 99.5 }
